Create one humorous Defeat illustration for the Urkaaaz match-result popup,
using the attached Green Frontier biome background.

## Reference inputs

- Attach the Green Frontier background image. Use it as the scene's
  environment reference and preserve its recognizable rolling terrain,
  greenery, lighting, and color palette.
- Use the existing shared panel at
  `assets_src/match/result-ui/match_result_popup_panel.png` to match the
  illustration window's framing and visual scale.
- Use the existing Victory illustration, if available, only as a reference
  for the shared rendering style and scale. The Defeat gag and pose must be
  clearly different.
- If a current in-game screenshot or blue Defender reference is available,
  use it to preserve the existing character design. Do not redesign the unit.

## Output

- Generate exactly one PNG:
  `match_result_defeat_illustration.png`.
- Save it under `assets_src/match/result-ui/`.
- Canvas: exactly 2024 x 698 pixels, landscape aspect ratio approximately
  2.9:1. This matches the transparent illustration opening in the supplied
  2400 x 1680 panel asset at its 4x source scale (about 506 x 175 dp).
- Fill the canvas edge-to-edge as a complete illustration for the opening.
  Do not add transparent margins, a panel frame, or a title plaque.
- Compose for the wide, shallow window: keep the Defender and leaf-pile gag
  large enough to read at popup size, with important details away from edges.

## Selected humorous scene

- Show the recognizable blue Defender sitting safely and upright in a soft
  pile of Green Frontier leaves after a defeat.
- Tilt the Defender's helmet slightly askew and give the character a sheepish,
  good-natured expression, as if pretending the leaf pile was intentional.
- Keep the pose comfortable and harmless. The joke is the absurdly cozy
  landing and the Defender's dignified reaction, not pain, injury, or
  humiliation.
- Use scattered leaves and soft grass to connect the gag to Green Frontier.
  Do not repeat Victory's airborne leaf-confetti gag.

## Composition and style

- Match the polished Urkaaaz fantasy-game art style and the canonical
  appearance of existing characters and equipment.
- Preserve the attached Green Frontier environment as the visual basis;
  adapt its crop or paint details only as needed to fit the wide opening.
- Make the Defender the clear focal point. Keep the leaf pile low in the
  composition so the face, tilted helmet, and expression remain visible.
- Avoid important details in the top edge, where the popup's title plaque
  visually overlaps the illustration window.
- Use lighting and contrast that remain clear beneath the popup's dimming
  scrim and inside the bronze frame.
- Keep the scene free of text and readable at the final display size.

## Runtime separation

- This is illustration artwork only. Do not include `DEFEAT`, level or biome
  labels, buttons, rewards, coins, unlocks, numbers, or UI.
- Do not draw the popup panel, title plaque, or any border; Android layers
  those assets independently.
- Do not add a new character, unit, faction, spell, weapon, or canonical lore.
- Do not include Victory, a new gameplay ability, gore, injury, or hostile
  imagery.

## Negative prompt

text, letters, numbers, labels, logo, watermark, signature, UI, buttons,
popup panel, title plaque, reward, coin, unlock, new unit, new weapon, new
spell, invented faction, invented lore, gore, injury, pain, humiliating pose,
crying, defeated character being mocked, airborne leaf confetti, generic
fantasy landscape, snow, desert, marsh, ashland, unrelated biome, cropped
character, tiny unreadable character, excessive particles, excessive glow

## Review checklist

- Confirm one 2024 x 698 PNG exists at the requested path.
- Confirm the composition fills the wide illustration window without adding
  a frame, title, or UI.
- Confirm the attached Green Frontier background is recognizable in the
  environment and palette.
- Confirm the blue Defender matches the existing appearance and remains the
  clear focal point.
- Confirm the seated leaf-pile gag is playful, safe, and distinct from Victory.
- Preview at approximately 506 x 175 dp inside the shared popup panel.
- Do not import the generated illustration into Android until it is reviewed
  and approved.
